--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIS IS A PRELIMINARY DESIGN TOOL, NOT A DESIGN AUTHORITY.

Its outputs are conceptual-design estimates carrying measured errors that are
published rather than hidden: see docs/ACCURACY.md. In particular, the jettison drop
zones (docs/DROP_ZONES.md) are NOT a range-safety product and must not be used to
clear any area. Nothing in this tool is qualified for flight, for range safety, or
for any decision affecting human safety or property.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The source code depends on, but does not include, the following packages, each under
its own licence: NumPy, SciPy, matplotlib, openpyxl and PyYAML (BSD-style or MIT),
and optionally CadQuery (Apache-2.0). Their licences govern their own code.

The Windows desktop app built by tools/build_app.py does include those packages and
their own dependencies, together with pywebview (BSD-3-Clause), pythonnet (MIT) and
the PyInstaller bootloader (GPL-2.0 with an exception that permits distribution). Their
licence notices are in the app's third_party_licenses folder. The app uses, but does
not include, Microsoft Edge WebView2.

The engineering methods implemented here are attributed in
outputs/engineering_method_register.xlsx. Methods drawn from Edberg & Costa,
"Design of Rockets and Space Launch Vehicles", 2nd ed. (AIAA, 2022) are cited to
their page and equation; that book is the authors' and publisher's copyright and is
not reproduced here.
